{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785178497810,"sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_FqsFt4CJ3mfEURhgYJV03Ezr","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-doc/019-skill-routing-refactor/021-skill-metadata-json-unification/research/lineages/sol-high-fast/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Deep Research Strategy: Root-Level Skill Metadata JSON Contract\n2: \n3: ## 2. TOPIC\n4: Establish the consumer-derived contract for root-level metadata JSON files across all 12 `.opencode/skills/` roots, without inspecting nested packet/mode metadata as fleet members and without conflating skill metadata with spec-folder continuity metadata.\n5: \n6: <!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n7: ## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n8: - [x] What is the complete 12-skill by eight-file root-level census, and who produces each file type?\n9: - [x] What schema and complete consumer call-site set governs each file type, including advisor, benchmark, doctor, and tests?\n10: - [x] What consumer-derived skill class taxonomy maps all 12 skills and makes each presence difference either required, optional by class, or defective?\n11: - [x] How should the five graph-only skills, `leaf-aliases.json`, `command-metadata.json`, and sparse `sk-git` be classified after behavior-impact checks?\n12: - [x] Where should the canonical contract live in `sk-doc/create-skill`, what can be generated/backfilled, and what fleet-wide presence-plus-freshness gate should enforce it?\n13: \n14: <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n15: \n16: ## 4. NON-GOALS\n17: - Do not implement or backfill metadata.\n18: - Do not treat nested mode/packet JSON as fleet root metadata.\n19: - Do not conflate `.opencode/skills/**/{description,graph-metadata}.json` with `.opencode/specs/**` continuity schemas.\n20: - Do not modify researched source files.\n21: \n22: ## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n23: - Stop at 10 iterations.\n24: - Stop earlier only after at least three evidence iterations, all five key questions are evidence-backed, the census covers all 12 skills and eight file types, disputed cases are resolved, and citations cover producers, consumers, schemas, and tests.\n25: \n26: <!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n27: ## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n28: - What is the complete 12-skill by eight-file root-level census, and who produces each file type?\n29: - What schema and complete consumer call-site set governs each file type, including advisor, benchmark, doctor, and tests?\n30: - What consumer-derived skill class taxonomy maps all 12 skills and makes each presence difference either required, optional by class, or defective?\n31: - How should the five graph-only skills, `leaf-aliases.json`, `command-metadata.json`, and sparse `sk-git` be classified after behavior-impact checks?\n32: - Where should the canonical contract live in `sk-doc/create-skill`, what can be generated/backfilled, and what fleet-wide presence-plus-freshness gate should enforce it?\n33: \n34: <!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n35: \n36: <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n37: <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n38: ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n39: - exact direct-child globbing produced a scope-safe census without admitting nested packet metadata; focused source reads then separated scaffold outputs, generated artifacts, and authored inputs. (iteration 1)\n40: - owner-scoped searches followed by implementation reads separated real file reads from thousands of continuity/docs mentions and exposed the direct-versus-indirect advisor boundary. (iteration 2)\n41: - executable-extension searches avoided the blocked prose/spec noise, while owner-focused reads exposed direct versus indirect consumers and the file-versus-surface cardinality distinction. (iteration 3)\n42: - consumer obligations reduced eight presence columns to two classes plus narrow overlays, allowing the census to expose defects rather than define classes. (iteration 4)\n43: - starting from the reducer's two-class model made missing-output discovery the first gate step, while focused reads of the authoring and enforcement surfaces exposed exactly where current presence-driven opt-ins fail. (iteration 5)\n44: \n45: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n46: \n47: <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n48: ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n49: - broad `command-metadata.json` search output was too large because repository-wide references include large records; narrowed producer searches were clean but yielded only negative evidence. (iteration 1)\n50: - broad exact-filename searches overflowed because identical names occur throughout spec packets and archived evidence. (iteration 2)\n51: - the prompt's expected four-consumer count did not match direct reader files because it implicitly grouped the validator and its test; treating the number literally would omit evidence. (iteration 3)\n52: - the freshness gate could not test missing-manifest eligibility because it discovers only committed manifests. (iteration 4)\n53: - broad integration searches overflowed on historical packet records; narrower package-script and executable-owner searches established the relevant negative evidence without repeating the blocked repository-wide approach. (iteration 5)\n54: \n55: <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n56: \n57: <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n58: ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n59: ### A broad `command-metadata.json` search produced oversized output; narrowing to the create-command and command trees found no producer. Future work should search its consumers and Git history rather than repeat the broad search. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n60: - What was tried: A broad `command-metadata.json` search produced oversized output; narrowing to the create-command and command trees found no producer. Future work should search its consumers and Git history rather than repeat the broad search.\n61: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n62: - Do NOT retry: A broad `command-metadata.json` search produced oversized output; narrowing to the create-command and command trees found no producer. Future work should search its consumers and Git history rather than repeat the broad search.\n63: \n64: ### A generic command-metadata backfill remains unjustified because there is no fleet production consumer or shared schema to generate toward. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/command-binding-existence.vitest.ts:44-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-design/shared/scripts/design-command-surface-check.mjs:121-180] -- BLOCKED (iteration 5, 1 attempts)\n65: - What was tried: A generic command-metadata backfill remains unjustified because there is no fleet production consumer or shared schema to generate toward. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/command-binding-existence.vitest.ts:44-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-design/shared/scripts/design-command-surface-check.mjs:121-180]\n66: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n67: - Do NOT retry: A generic command-metadata backfill remains unjustified because there is no fleet production consumer or shared schema to generate toward. [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/system-skill-advisor/mcp-server/tests/command-binding-existence.vitest.ts:44-64] [SOURCE: .opencode/skills/sk-design/shared/scripts/design-command-surface-check.mjs:121-180]\n68: \n69: ### Counting `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, or `tsconfig.json`: they are root JSON files but not among the eight named metadata types. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n70: - What was tried: Counting `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, or `tsconfig.json`: they are root JSON files but not among the eight named metadata types.\n71: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n72: - Do NOT retry: Counting `package.json`, `package-lock.json`, or `tsconfig.json`: they are root JSON files but not among the eight named metadata types.\n73: \n74: ### Counting nested mode/packet JSON: excluded by the focus contract and direct-child glob. -- BLOCKED (iteration 1, 1 attempts)\n75: - What was tried: Counting nested mode/packet JSON: excluded by the focus contract and direct-child glob.\n76: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n77: - Do NOT retry: Counting nested mode/packet JSON: excluded by the focus contract and direct-child glob.\n78: \n79: ### Counting only four direct reader files is stale: there are five; four is defensible only as the number of consumer surfaces after grouping a validator with its unit test. [INFERENCE: exact executable search results reconciled with the five reader files cited in Finding 5] -- BLOCKED (iteration 3, 1 attempts)\n80: - What was tried: Counting only four direct reader files is stale: there are five; four is defensible only as the number of consumer surfaces after grouping a validator with its unit test. [INFERENCE: exact executable search results reconciled with the five reader files cited in Finding 5]\n81: - Why blocked: Repeated iteration evidence ruled this direction out.\n82: - Do NOT retry: Counting only four direct reader files is stale: there are five; four is defensible only as the number of consumer surfaces after grouping a validator with its unit test. [INFERENCE: exact executable search results reconciled with the five reader files cited in Finding 5]\n83: \n84: ### Creating a third sparse class for `sk-git`: class-first discovery makes it a failing S root and exposes the three missing files. [SOURCE: research/lineages/sol-high-fast/iterations/iteration-004.md:15-15] -- BLOCKED (iteration 5, 1 attempts)\n85: - What was tried: Creating a