{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785178597417,"sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_d0Kszv4tLmulwvY6NgNgi5JW","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json\n+{\n+  \"topic\": \"Determine which git operations warrant a preflight advisory in a PreToolUse Bash hook, what pre-execution state each candidate rule can evaluate, and where the noise threshold sits.\",\n+  \"maxIterations\": 5,\n+  \"minIterations\": 3,\n+  \"convergenceThreshold\": 0.05,\n+  \"antiConvergence\": {\n+    \"minIterations\": 3,\n+    \"convergenceMode\": \"default\",\n+    \"stopPolicy\": \"max-iterations\"\n+  },\n+  \"stopPolicy\": \"max-iterations\",\n+  \"stuckThreshold\": 3,\n+  \"maxDurationMinutes\": 120,\n+  \"maxToolCallsPerIteration\": 12,\n+  \"maxMinutesPerIteration\": 10,\n+  \"progressiveSynthesis\": false,\n+  \"specFolder\": \".opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research\",\n+  \"fanout_lineage_artifact_dir\": \".opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol\",\n+  \"resource_map_present\": false,\n+  \"resource_map\": {\n+    \"emit\": true\n+  },\n+  \"createdAt\": \"2026-07-27T18:55:37Z\",\n+  \"status\": \"initialized\",\n+  \"executionMode\": \"auto\",\n+  \"executor\": {\n+    \"kind\": \"cli-opencode\",\n+    \"type\": \"cli-opencode\",\n+    \"model\": \"openai/gpt-5.6-sol\",\n+    \"reasoningEffort\": null,\n+    \"serviceTier\": null,\n+    \"sandboxMode\": null,\n+    \"timeoutSeconds\": 900\n+  },\n+  \"lineage\": {\n+    \"sessionId\": \"fanout-sol-1785178337201-eaydo6\",\n+    \"parentSessionId\": null,\n+    \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n+    \"generation\": 1,\n+    \"continuedFromRun\": null\n+  },\n+  \"fileProtection\": {\n+    \"deep-research-config.json\": \"immutable\",\n+    \"deep-research-state.jsonl\": \"append-only\",\n+    \"deep-research-strategy.md\": \"mutable\",\n+    \"deep-research-dashboard.md\": \"auto-generated\",\n+    \"findings-registry.json\": \"auto-generated\",\n+    \"iteration-*.md\": \"write-once\",\n+    \"research.md\": \"mutable\"\n+  }\n+}\n*** Add File: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl\n+{\"type\":\"config\",\"topic\":\"Determine which git operations warrant a preflight advisory in a PreToolUse Bash hook, what pre-execution state each candidate rule can evaluate, and where the noise threshold sits.\",\"maxIterations\":5,\"minIterations\":3,\"convergenceThreshold\":0.05,\"antiConvergence\":{\"convergenceMode\":\"default\"},\"stopPolicy\":\"max-iterations\",\"resource_map_present\":false,\"resource_map\":{\"emit\":true},\"createdAt\":\"2026-07-27T18:55:37Z\",\"specFolder\":\".opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research\",\"artifactDir\":\".opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol\",\"sessionId\":\"fanout-sol-1785178337201-eaydo6\",\"generation\":1,\"executor\":{\"kind\":\"cli-opencode\",\"model\":\"openai/gpt-5.6-sol\",\"reasoningEffort\":null},\"nextRunAt\":null,\"remainingDelayMs\":null}\n*** Add File: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n+# Deep Research Strategy: Git Preflight Advisory Rules\n+\n+## 2. TOPIC\n+Determine which git invocation shapes justify a one-line pre-execution advisory, which repository and command state is genuinely available before execution, and which candidate rules remain quiet enough to preserve operator attention.\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n+## 3. KEY QUESTIONS (remaining)\n+- [ ] Which git operation families can be classified reliably from the Bash command before execution?\n+- [ ] Which repository, worktree, index, remote, config, and account state is genuinely available before each candidate command runs?\n+- [ ] Which high-cost failures beyond the five observed incidents warrant new advisory rules?\n+- [ ] How often would each candidate fire in real repository history, and what is the defensible noise threshold?\n+- [ ] Which dangerous-looking operations should remain silent because enforcement already owns them or preflight state is unavailable/too noisy?\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n+\n+## 4. NON-GOALS\n+- Do not implement or modify the evaluator, hook, sk-git rules, or frontmatter.\n+- Do not redesign the advisory mechanism.\n+- Do not turn advisory findings into blocking rules.\n+- Do not claim post-execution outcomes are pre-evaluable.\n+- Do not write outside this detached lineage directory.\n+\n+## 5. STOP CONDITIONS\n+- Run exactly five iterations; convergence before iteration five is telemetry only.\n+- Stop after iteration five when candidate operations include exact invocation shapes, genuinely available pre-state, measured or explicitly unmeasured noise, source classification, and confirmed/inferred confidence.\n+- Preserve eliminated high-noise and non-pre-evaluable alternatives as primary negative knowledge.\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n+## 6. ANSWERED QUESTIONS\n+[None yet]\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:answered-questions -->\n+\n+<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: START -->\n+<!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n+## 7. WHAT WORKED\n+[None yet]\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n+## 8. WHAT FAILED\n+[None yet]\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n+## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n+[None yet]\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n+## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n+[None yet]\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n+## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n+- Completed pivots: 0\n+- Failed pivots: 0\n+- Audited overrides: 0\n+- Saturated: none yet\n+- Pivot lineage: none yet\n+- Remaining frontier: operation inventory, destructive history, staging/commit semantics, coordination/remotes, noise calibration\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n+## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n+[None yet]\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n+\n+<!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n+## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n+Inventory command-classifiable git operation families and map each to pre-execution state that can actually be read before execution.\n+<!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n+<!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n+\n+## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n+- The briefing's five incidents are a floor, not the answer.\n+- Existing evaluator checks are pure command-string predicates and `sk-git` currently declares no `hard_rules`.\n+- Every usable finding must include operation, pre-execution state and availability, measured or explicitly unmeasured noise, source, and confidence.\n+- `resource-map.md` is absent; coverage comes from local source, Git history, and exact repository-state measurements.\n+- The code graph is empty, so exact Grep, Read, Glob, and bounded Git evidence are authoritative.\n+\n+## 13. RESEARCH BOUNDARIES\n+- Max iterations: 5\n+- Stop policy: max-iterations\n+- Convergence threshold: 0.05 telemetry only before iteration 5\n+- Executor: `cli-opencode`, model `openai/gpt-5.6-sol`\n+- Allowed writes: this detached lineage directory only\n+- Progressive synthesis: false; phase synthesis owns `research.md`\n*** Add File: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n+{\n+  \"sessionId\": \"fanout-sol-1785178337201-eaydo6\",\n+  \"parentSessionId\": null,\n+  \"lineageMode\": \"new\",\n+  \"generation\": 1,\n+  \"continuedFromRun\": null,\n+  \"keyQuestions\": [],\n+  \"openQuestions\": [],\n+  \"resolvedQuestions\": [],\n+  \"carriedForwardOpenQuestions\": [],\n+  