{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785180435824,"sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"task","callID":"call_whsd4gwkMwuakX8BuiFi3QM5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Research staging commit semantics","subagent_type":"deep-research","command":"/deep:research:auto","prompt":"Execute exactly ONE deep-research LEAF iteration for the detached lineage. No subagents.\n\nIteration: 3 of 5\nFocus: Investigate staging and commit semantics: broad `git add`, `git commit -a`, `git commit --only`, pathspec expansion, partial rename staging, pre-commit index mutation, and cheap probes that distinguish intentional multi-path work from cross-session contamination. The briefing's add-directory and commit--only incidents are a floor; identify missed cases and noisy false friends.\n\nRead the lineage config, state, strategy, registry, iterations 001-002, and BRIEFING.md before research. Primary evidence should include sk-git commit workflows, actual Git help/status/diff semantics, current hooks, evaluator constraints, and bounded repository history/state where useful.\n\nEvery finding MUST contain exact operation shape; specific pre-execution state; genuine pre-run availability; measured real-history noise or explicit not measured; source classification (named rule, observed incident, or new with justification); confirmed/inferred confidence. Explicitly separate what PreToolUse can know from what pre-commit hooks can mutate later. Recommend silence when ownership is unknowable or a rule would fire constantly.\n\nAllowed writes only:\n- .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md\n- append one canonical iteration record to .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl\n- .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-003.jsonl\n\nDo not edit any other path. Do not stage or commit. Include canonical route proof and required metadata, then verify all three artifacts."},"output":"<task id=\"ses_05afb91faffeJCwJyzuoRdBriS\" state=\"completed\">\n<task_result>\n## Iteration 3 Complete\n\n**Focus**: Staging and commit semantics, path selection, hook-time mutation boundaries, and contamination probes  \n**Findings**: 9 findings (4 new, 5 partially new, 0 redundant)  \n**newInfoRatio**: 0.72  \n**Questions answered**: Objective staging/commit mismatch detection without inferring path ownership  \n**Questions remaining**: 4  \n**Edge cases**: Missing exact argv telemetry and ownership metadata  \n**Recommended next focus**: Detached/linked-worktree pushes, primary-checkout reconciliation, account/remote ownership, and refspec risks\n\n**Files written**:\n- `research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md`\n- `research/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl` — appended exactly one record\n- `research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-003.jsonl`\n\n**Verification**:\n- All three artifacts exist: yes\n- JSONL iteration append count: 1\n- Delta/state canonical records match: yes\n- Nine findings fully cited: yes\n- Required metadata and route proof: yes\n- Packet boundary respected: yes\n- Reducer-owned files untouched: yes\n- Files staged or committed: none\n\n**Status**: complete\n</task_result>\n</task>","metadata":{"parentSessionId":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","sessionId":"ses_05afb91faffeJCwJyzuoRdBriS","model":{"modelID":"gpt-5.6-sol","providerID":"openai"},"truncated":false},"title":"Research staging commit semantics","time":{"start":1785179958982,"end":1785180435819}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_06e5ed0043614e54016a67af2ebd20819196bf29095235d7d7"}},"id":"prt_fa5044ea6001o9OuJMGdJE3klS","sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","messageID":"msg_fa50441ad001m1SXijsNzX9PhV"}}
