{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1785180451209,"sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","part":{"id":"prt_fa50bf187001Dz53fNhBPWWwzh","messageID":"msg_fa50be474001Jaj3zMJT0GwzQI","sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785180487847,"sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_J6t0fmj2Z5QQ9vEL4ViIG3Zz","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n@@\n - Exact installed-Git help plus current-state probes separated destructive intent from routine forms already protected by Git and quantified current exposure without mutating state. (iteration 2)\n+- Combining official selection semantics, native dry runs, current hooks, and 500-commit path breadth produced objective mismatch predicates without inventing session ownership. (iteration 3)\n@@\n ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n@@\n - Repeating reflog measurement could not recover flags, pathspecs, failures, or final state-gated fire rates; remote containment can prove known publication but not non-publication. (iteration 2)\n+- Ordinary history cannot recover add/commit options or hook-time snapshots, and Git state has no session-owner field. (iteration 3)\n@@\n - Generic destructive-family warnings and recovery/control forms: exact state gates or Git's own protections make them unnecessary. (iteration 2)\n+- Path-count, top-level spread, and generic selective-commit warnings: sampled history shows they are common and do not prove contamination. (iteration 3)\n@@\n - Ordinary `branch -d`, checked-out branch deletion, ordinary worktree removal/prune, staged-only restore, clean/prune dry runs, routine GC, and rebase recovery forms. (iteration 2)\n+- Predicting interactive/stdin-generated path selections, treating `--include` as suspicious, inferring ownership, or claiming the pre-hook candidate is the final commit tree. (iteration 3)\n@@\n - Which staging and commit predicates detect cross-session contamination without warning on intentional multi-path commits? (iteration 2)\n+- Which positive local coordination and remote/account facts justify advisories despite unavoidable race windows? (iteration 3)\n@@\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Investigate staging and commit semantics: broad `git add`, `git commit -a`, `git commit --only`, pathspec expansion, partial rename staging, pre-commit index mutation, and cheap probes that distinguish intentional multi-path work from cross-session contamination.\n+Investigate worktree, remote, and account coordination: detached/linked-worktree pushes, primary-checkout reconciliation, autosync bypass, active `gh` account versus remote owner, force/delete/tag refspecs, and exact preflight race/noise boundaries.\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n@@\n     \"How often do state-gated candidates match without exact argv telemetry?\",\n-    \"Which staging and commit predicates detect cross-session contamination without warning on intentional multi-path commits?\"\n+    \"Which staging and commit predicates detect cross-session contamination without warning on intentional multi-path commits?\",\n+    \"Which positive local coordination and remote/account facts justify advisories despite unavoidable race windows?\"\n@@\n     {\n       \"id\": \"f2-built-in-safety\",\n       \"iteration\": 2,\n       \"text\": \"Routine and recovery forms should stay silent where Git already blocks or preserves state, including branch -d, checked-out branch deletion, ordinary dirty worktree removal, clean without force, and conflicted stash pop.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"f3-selection-mismatch\",\n+      \"iteration\": 3,\n+      \"text\": \"Retain staging advisories only when exact broad/selective commands expose objective mismatches: held-back staged paths, one-sided inferred renames, forced ignored files, or reproducible expansion beyond explicit paths.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"f3-no-ownership\",\n+      \"iteration\": 3,\n+      \"text\": \"Git state has no session-owner field and PreToolUse sees only the pre-hook candidate, so advisories must be neutral and cannot guarantee final commit contents.\"\n@@\n     ,\"Using absent remote containment as proof that history is unpublished\"\n+    ,\"Path-count-only, cross-top-level, and unconditional selective-commit warnings\"\n+    ,\"Predicting interactive or stdin path selections and hook-time final commit state\"\n@@\n-    \"iterationsCompleted\": 2,\n+    \"iterationsCompleted\": 3,\n@@\n-    \"keyFindings\": 22,\n-    \"convergenceScore\": 0.6,\n-    \"coverageBySources\": {\"code\": 17, \"history\": 8, \"state\": 10}\n+    \"keyFindings\": 31,\n+    \"convergenceScore\": 0.72,\n+    \"coverageBySources\": {\"code\": 24, \"history\": 13, \"state\": 17, \"web\": 1}\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\nM .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -33,28 +33,32 @@\n <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n - Pairing exact sk-git rules and hook coverage with a bounded 1,482-entry HEAD reflog separated command risk from broad-family prevalence. (iteration 1)\n - Exact installed-Git help plus current-state probes separated destructive intent from routine forms already protected by Git and quantified current exposure without mutating state. (iteration 2)\n+- Combining official selection semantics, native dry runs, current hooks, and 500-commit path breadth produced objective mismatch predicates without inventing session ownership. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n - Git history cannot recover option-sensitive invocation frequency or failed commands because it records ref outcomes rather than complete argv. (iteration 1)\n - Repeating reflog measurement could not recover flags, pathspecs, failures, or final state-gated fire rates; remote containment can prove known publication but not non-publication. (iteration 2)\n+- Ordinary history cannot recover add/commit options or hook-time snapshots, and Git state has no session-owner field. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n - Generic warnings for every commit, reset, rebase, pull, or push: broad-family prevalence and existing enforcement make them noisy. (iteration 1)\n - Treating Git log/reflog as exact shell-command telemetry: flags, pathspecs, and failed commands are absent. (iteration 1)\n - Generic destructive-family warnings and recovery/control forms: exact state gates or Git's own protections make them unnecessary. (iteration 2)\n+- Path-count, top-level spread, and generic selective-commit warnings: sampled history shows they are common and do not prove contamination. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n - Duplicate advisories for pre-push naming and non-allowlisted push permission already owned by blocking enforcement. (iteration 1)\n - Treating remote snapshots, push authorization, conflict outcomes, or post-hook commit contents as guaranteed pre-execution facts. (iteration 1)\n - Ordinary `branch -d`, checked-out branch deletion, ordinary worktree removal/prune, staged-only restore, clean/prune dry runs, routine GC, and rebase recovery forms. (iteration 2)\n+- Predicting interactive/stdin-generated path selections, treating `--include` as suspicious, inferring ownership, or claiming the pre-hook candidate is the final commit tree. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n@@ -70,13 +74,14 @@\n ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n - Which bounded state probes make published amend/rebase, destructive overwrite, branch/worktree deletion, and remote/tag force/delete predicates precise enough? (iteration 1)\n - How often do state-gated candidates match, given that ordinary Git history cannot provide exact argv telemetry? (iteration 1)\n - Which staging and commit predicates detect cross-session contamination without warning on intentional multi-path commits? (iteration 2)\n+- Which positive local coordination and remote/account facts justify advisories despite unavoidable race windows? (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Investigate staging and commit semantics: broad `git add`, `git commit -a`, `git commit --only`, pathspec expansion, partial rename staging, pre-commit index mutation, and cheap probes that distinguish intentional multi-path work from cross-session contamination.\n+Investigate worktree, remote, and account coordination: detached/linked-worktree pushes, primary-checkout reconciliation, autosync bypass, active `gh` account versus remote owner, force/delete/tag refspecs, and exact preflight race/noise boundaries.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n \n ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n\nIndex: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n@@ -36,9 +36,10 @@\n   \"resolvedQuestions\": [\"q-operation-families\"],\n   \"carriedForwardOpenQuestions\": [\n     \"Which bounded state probes make destructive-history predicates precise enough?\",\n     \"How often do state-gated candidates match without exact argv telemetry?\",\n-    \"Which staging and commit predicates detect cross-session contamination without warning on intentional multi-path commits?\"\n+    \"Which staging and commit predicates detect cross-session contamination without warning on intentional multi-path commits?\",\n+    \"Which positive local coordination and remote/account facts justify advisories despite unavoidable race windows?\"\n   ],\n   \"uncoveredQuestions\": [],\n   \"keyFindings\": [\n     {\n@@ -59,8 +60,18 @@\n     {\n       \"id\": \"f2-built-in-safety\",\n       \"iteration\": 2,\n       \"text\": \"Routine and recovery forms should stay silent where Git already blocks or preserves state, including branch -d, checked-out branch deletion, ordinary dirty worktree removal, clean without force, and conflicted stash pop.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"f3-selection-mismatch\",\n+      \"iteration\": 3,\n+      \"text\": \"Retain staging advisories only when exact broad/selective commands expose objective mismatches: held-back staged paths, one-sided inferred renames, forced ignored files, or reproducible expansion beyond explicit paths.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"f3-no-ownership\",\n+      \"iteration\": 3,\n+      \"text\": \"Git state has no session-owner field and PreToolUse sees only the pre-hook candidate, so advisories must be neutral and cannot guarantee final commit contents.\"\n     }\n   ],\n   \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n     \"Unconditional warnings for generic commit, reset, rebase, pull, or push\",\n@@ -68,14 +79,16 @@\n     \"Using Git history as exact argv telemetry\",\n     \"Treating raceable remote snapshots or post-execution outcomes as facts\"\n     ,\"Generic destructive-family and recovery-form warnings\"\n     ,\"Using absent remote containment as proof that history is unpublished\"\n+    ,\"Path-count-only, cross-top-level, and unconditional selective-commit warnings\"\n+    ,\"Predicting interactive or stdin path selections and hook-time final commit state\"\n   ],\n   \"metrics\": {\n-    \"iterationsCompleted\": 2,\n+    \"iterationsCompleted\": 3,\n     \"openQuestions\": 4,\n     \"resolvedQuestions\": 1,\n-    \"keyFindings\": 22,\n-    \"convergenceScore\": 0.6,\n-    \"coverageBySources\": {\"code\": 17, \"history\": 8, \"state\": 10}\n+    \"keyFindings\": 31,\n+    \"convergenceScore\": 0.72,\n+    \"coverageBySources\": {\"code\": 24, \"history\": 13, \"state\": 17, \"web\": 1}\n   }\n }\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","relativePath":".opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -33,28 +33,32 @@\n <!-- ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n ## 7. WHAT WORKED\n - Pairing exact sk-git rules and hook coverage with a bounded 1,482-entry HEAD reflog separated command risk from broad-family prevalence. (iteration 1)\n - Exact installed-Git help plus current-state probes separated destructive intent from routine forms already protected by Git and quantified current exposure without mutating state. (iteration 2)\n+- Combining official selection semantics, native dry runs, current hooks, and 500-commit path breadth produced objective mismatch predicates without inventing session ownership. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-worked -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n ## 8. WHAT FAILED\n - Git history cannot recover option-sensitive invocation frequency or failed commands because it records ref outcomes rather than complete argv. (iteration 1)\n - Repeating reflog measurement could not recover flags, pathspecs, failures, or final state-gated fire rates; remote containment can prove known publication but not non-publication. (iteration 2)\n+- Ordinary history cannot recover add/commit options or hook-time snapshots, and Git state has no session-owner field. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:what-failed -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n ## 9. EXHAUSTED APPROACHES (do not retry)\n - Generic warnings for every commit, reset, rebase, pull, or push: broad-family prevalence and existing enforcement make them noisy. (iteration 1)\n - Treating Git log/reflog as exact shell-command telemetry: flags, pathspecs, and failed commands are absent. (iteration 1)\n - Generic destructive-family warnings and recovery/control forms: exact state gates or Git's own protections make them unnecessary. (iteration 2)\n+- Path-count, top-level spread, and generic selective-commit warnings: sampled history shows they are common and do not prove contamination. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:exhausted-approaches -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n ## 10. RULED OUT DIRECTIONS\n - Duplicate advisories for pre-push naming and non-allowlisted push permission already owned by blocking enforcement. (iteration 1)\n - Treating remote snapshots, push authorization, conflict outcomes, or post-hook commit contents as guaranteed pre-execution facts. (iteration 1)\n - Ordinary `branch -d`, checked-out branch deletion, ordinary worktree removal/prune, staged-only restore, clean/prune dry runs, routine GC, and rebase recovery forms. (iteration 2)\n+- Predicting interactive/stdin-generated path selections, treating `--include` as suspicious, inferring ownership, or claiming the pre-hook candidate is the final commit tree. (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:ruled-out-directions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:divergence-frontier -->\n ## 10A. SATURATED DIRECTIONS AND DIVERGENCE FRONTIER\n@@ -70,13 +74,14 @@\n ## 11A. CARRIED-FORWARD OPEN QUESTIONS\n - Which bounded state probes make published amend/rebase, destructive overwrite, branch/worktree deletion, and remote/tag force/delete predicates precise enough? (iteration 1)\n - How often do state-gated candidates match, given that ordinary Git history cannot provide exact argv telemetry? (iteration 1)\n - Which staging and commit predicates detect cross-session contamination without warning on intentional multi-path commits? (iteration 2)\n+- Which positive local coordination and remote/account facts justify advisories despite unavoidable race windows? (iteration 3)\n <!-- /ANCHOR:carried-forward-open-questions -->\n \n <!-- ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Investigate staging and commit semantics: broad `git add`, `git commit -a`, `git commit --only`, pathspec expansion, partial rename staging, pre-commit index mutation, and cheap probes that distinguish intentional multi-path work from cross-session contamination.\n+Investigate worktree, remote, and account coordination: detached/linked-worktree pushes, primary-checkout reconciliation, autosync bypass, active `gh` account versus remote owner, force/delete/tag refspecs, and exact preflight race/noise boundaries.\n <!-- /ANCHOR:next-focus -->\n <!-- MACHINE-OWNED: END -->\n \n ## 12. KNOWN CONTEXT\n","additions":6,"deletions":1},{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json","relativePath":".opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json","type":"update","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n@@ -36,9 +36,10 @@\n   \"resolvedQuestions\": [\"q-operation-families\"],\n   \"carriedForwardOpenQuestions\": [\n     \"Which bounded state probes make destructive-history predicates precise enough?\",\n     \"How often do state-gated candidates match without exact argv telemetry?\",\n-    \"Which staging and commit predicates detect cross-session contamination without warning on intentional multi-path commits?\"\n+    \"Which staging and commit predicates detect cross-session contamination without warning on intentional multi-path commits?\",\n+    \"Which positive local coordination and remote/account facts justify advisories despite unavoidable race windows?\"\n   ],\n   \"uncoveredQuestions\": [],\n   \"keyFindings\": [\n     {\n@@ -59,8 +60,18 @@\n     {\n       \"id\": \"f2-built-in-safety\",\n       \"iteration\": 2,\n       \"text\": \"Routine and recovery forms should stay silent where Git already blocks or preserves state, including branch -d, checked-out branch deletion, ordinary dirty worktree removal, clean without force, and conflicted stash pop.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"f3-selection-mismatch\",\n+      \"iteration\": 3,\n+      \"text\": \"Retain staging advisories only when exact broad/selective commands expose objective mismatches: held-back staged paths, one-sided inferred renames, forced ignored files, or reproducible expansion beyond explicit paths.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"f3-no-ownership\",\n+      \"iteration\": 3,\n+      \"text\": \"Git state has no session-owner field and PreToolUse sees only the pre-hook candidate, so advisories must be neutral and cannot guarantee final commit contents.\"\n     }\n   ],\n   \"ruledOutDirections\": [\n     \"Unconditional warnings for generic commit, reset, rebase, pull, or push\",\n@@ -68,14 +79,16 @@\n     \"Using Git history as exact argv telemetry\",\n     \"Treating raceable remote snapshots or post-execution outcomes as facts\"\n     ,\"Generic destructive-family and recovery-form warnings\"\n     ,\"Using absent remote containment as proof that history is unpublished\"\n+    ,\"Path-count-only, cross-top-level, and unconditional selective-commit warnings\"\n+    ,\"Predicting interactive or stdin path selections and hook-time final commit state\"\n   ],\n   \"metrics\": {\n-    \"iterationsCompleted\": 2,\n+    \"iterationsCompleted\": 3,\n     \"openQuestions\": 4,\n     \"resolvedQuestions\": 1,\n-    \"keyFindings\": 22,\n-    \"convergenceScore\": 0.6,\n-    \"coverageBySources\": {\"code\": 17, \"history\": 8, \"state\": 10}\n+    \"keyFindings\": 31,\n+    \"convergenceScore\": 0.72,\n+    \"coverageBySources\": {\"code\": 24, \"history\": 13, \"state\": 17, \"web\": 1}\n   }\n }\n","additions":18,"deletions":5}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\nM .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json","time":{"start":1785180487840,"end":1785180487846}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_09856542af2c67ce016a67b12bd1f081919e91773d8d010d65"}},"id":"prt_fa50c24ea001URm2rJpjNqNCQh","sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","messageID":"msg_fa50be474001Jaj3zMJT0GwzQI"}}
