{"type":"text","timestamp":1785181557973,"sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","part":{"id":"prt_fa51cc367001QCiD9nh38I1uAX","messageID":"msg_fa51cb35f001y9TxP92s850RPv","sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","type":"text","text":"Five evidence passes are complete. The retained set is now being checked for required-field coverage and consolidated into the lineage synthesis; convergence did not shorten the forced-depth run.","time":{"start":1785181553511,"end":1785181557972},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0e9d49173a304904016a67b57175188191ad48276185a4f802","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785181558091,"sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_xqnXdDu1ICtxbgp2xPiqVpPB","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-005.md"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-005.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Iteration 5: Final Candidate Matrix and Noise Threshold\n2: \n3: ## Canonical Route Proof\n4: \n5: `Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research`; `agent_definition_loaded=true`; detached lineage `sol`; forced run/iteration `5 of 5`; `stopPolicy=max-iterations`; LEAF execution with no sub-agent dispatch.\n6: \n7: ## Focus\n8: \n9: Calibrate every candidate retained through iterations 1-4 into a decision-ready advisory rule set. Ranking uses four explicit dimensions: positive-evidence strength (`E3` exact command plus positive local state, `E2` exact command-only destructive/policy intent, `E1` raceable or heuristic positive snapshot), cost of the failure, overlap with a higher-ranked rule, and measured prevalence where Git history legitimately exposes it. Option-sensitive fire rates remain unmeasured because Git history contains ref outcomes, not complete argv, failed commands, or preflight-state matches. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md:44-58] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/BRIEFING.md:38-59]\n10: \n11: ## Findings\n12: \n13: 1. **The final retained set is 23 narrowly gated rules, not broad Git-family warnings.** Each row below supplies the exact operation, genuinely available pre-state, measured or explicitly unmeasured noise, source classification, confidence, harm cost, measured/expected probe cost, and coalescing overlap. [INFERENCE: based on the candidate validations in iterations 1-4 and the ranking criteria stated above]\n14: 2. **Fourteen candidate classes are rejected for unavailable predicates, existing protection, or excessive expected noise.** In particular, session ownership, post-fetch rewrite sets, Git transport identity, remote authorization, final push/commit outcomes, and interactive/stdin selections are not genuine pre-execution facts. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:31-47] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:33-50]\n15: 3. **Probe latency requires a tiered budget.** Five-run medians/maxima in the current checkout were: `rev-parse` 7.87/26.84 ms, ref inventory 10.15/13.71 ms, `--contains=HEAD` 15.71/36.59 ms, worktree list 15.72/39.68 ms, stash list 16.22/23.94 ms, diff 68.27/92.32 ms, rename diff 89.73/92.93 ms, reflog-expire dry-run 148.21/149.99 ms, clean dry-run 336.28/425.09 ms, add dry-run 438.31/505.34 ms, status 464.68/593.83 ms, commit dry-run 601.58/606.63 ms, and `clean -ndx` 1,630.21/3,254.80 ms. A 35-worktree status sweep took 20,147.45 ms and is rejected from the hot path. [SOURCE: bounded read-only Git benchmark captured 2026-07-27T19:41:12Z]\n16: 4. **The attention budget is measurable only with future normalized PreToolUse telemetry, so rollout must begin in shadow mode.** Target `<0.5` emitted alerts per 100 direct Git invocations per rule, hard ceiling `1/100`; target `<2/100` aggregate, hard ceiling `3/100`, after one-line coalescing and a minimum 500 eligible invocations or 30 days. These are design targets, not observed rates. The repository proxy shows why: amend outcomes were 0.47%, rebase 2.96%, reset 13.53%, and commit 73.55%; 90.6% of 500 commits were multi-path. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:9-17] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:13-29] [INFERENCE: broad-family rates above the aggregate budget require positive state gates]\n17: 5. **One-line coalescing is the release contract, not a presentation preference.** Emit at most one line for the whole Bash invocation, at most two positive facts plus `+N`, in priority order `irrecoverable local loss > shared/remote rewrite > selection mismatch > coordination`; reuse probe results and suppress lower-ranked overlaps and enforcement-owned messages. Format: `Advisory: <operation> — <primary fact>; <secondary fact>[; +N].` Cap at 180 characters and never print raw URLs, credentials, or file contents. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/BRIEFING.md:52-59] [INFERENCE: one line and priority suppression keep aggregate attention cost bounded when one command matches several predicates]\n18: \n19: ## Retained Candidate Matrix (ranked)\n20: \n21: The rows absorb every retained candidate from iterations 1-4; variants are grouped only when they share the same predicate and remediation.\n22: \n23: | Rank | Candidate and exact operation | Pre-state and genuine availability | Noise / source / confidence | Cost, probe, overlap |\n24: |---:|---|---|---|---|\n25: | 1 | **Hook bypass:** direct `git commit ... --no-verify` or `git push ... --no-verify`. | Exact parsed option; command-only and genuinely available for direct Git. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. Named sk-git NEVER #9; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:10-12] | Critical because it removes enforcement; zero Git probes; coalesce with any lower rule but never suppress. |\n26: | 2 | **Direct branch creation:** `git branch <new>`, `checkout -b|-B`, or `switch -c|-C`. | Exact direct command; optional branch/worktree existence is local. Opaque aliases/scripts unavailable. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. Named NEVER #2; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:10-10] | High process/collision cost; command-only or ~16 ms worktree probe; no enforcement overlap found. |\n27: | 3 | **Published amend:** `git commit ... --amend`. | Positive containment of `HEAD` by a remote-tracking or integration ref is local and available; absence never proves unpublished. | Broad amend proxy 7/1,486 = **0.47%**; gated subset **unmeasured**. Named NEVER #10; local predicate **confirmed**, publication completeness **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:9-9] | Critical shared-history rewrite; ~16 ms containment; overlaps path/`-a` amend and wins coalescing. |\n28: | 4 | **Hard reset with positive loss:** `git reset --hard [<target>]`. | Exact target plus nonempty index/worktree overwrite or positive branch-tip retreat relative to other durable refs; locally available snapshot. | Broad reset proxy 201/1,486 = **13.53%**; hard/state-gated rate **unmeasured**. New extension of ALWAYS #15; predicate **confirmed**, durable-ref valuation **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:13-13] | Critical local loss; diff ~68 ms plus refs ~10 ms; wins over generic restore/history-loss facts. |\n29: | 5 | **Forced clean with actual removals:** `git clean -f|-ff` preserving `-d`, `-x|-X`, exclusions, and pathspec; exclude dry-run. | Native equivalent `git clean -n...` returns at least one removal; exact selection is genuinely available but raceable. | Invocation/fire rate **unmeasured**. New; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:15-15] | Critical untracked/ignored loss; 336-425 ms normally, `-x` 1.63-3.25 s exceptional tier; coalesce removal count only. |\n30: | 6 | **Forced removal of a dirty/live worktree:** `git worktree remove -f|--force <path>`. | Exact target registration/status and positive live wrapper PID; local and available. Missing marker is unknown, not inactive. | Invocation rate **unmeasured**; current exposure 20 dirty of 35 worktrees. Named ALWAYS #17; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:21-21] | Critical local/session loss; inspect only target, never 20.15 s all-worktree sweep; overlaps branch deletion and wins. |\n31: | 7 | **Unrescued stash destruction:** `git stash drop [<stash>]` or `git stash clear`. | Resolve selected SHA(s), rescue/durable refs, and count entries lacking rescue; local and available, selector race acknowledged. | Invocation rate **unmeasured**; current exposure 20 stash entries, none directly rescued. ALWAYS #14 extension; availability **confirmed**, durable suppression **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:23-23] | Critical recovery loss; stash/ref probes ~16/10 ms; coalesce with expiry/prune as one recovery warning. |\n32: | 8 | **Immediate reflog expiry with nonempty dry-run:** `git reflog expire --expire=now|--expire-unreachable=now ...`; exclude `--dry-run`. | Native `--dry-run --verbose` for selected refs; local snapshot genuinely available. | Invocation rate **unmeasured**; 390 reflog-only commits were an exposure count, not fire rate. New; **confirmed** for dry-run, importance **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:25-25] | Critical recovery-pointer loss; ~148-150 ms; coalesce with immediate prune. |\n33: | 9 | **Immediate object pruning:** `git gc --prune=now`, effective `gc.pruneExpire=now`, or `git prune --expire=now`; exclude dry-run/routine forms. | Exact token/effective config is genuinely available; exact future deletion set and concurrent-writer safety are not required or claimable. | Invocation rate **unmeasured**; prior 87,410 unreachable objects is exposure only. New; command/config **confirmed**, consequence set **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:27-27] | Critical recovery-window collapse; command/config only—do not run `fsck`/full reachability; suppressed into rank 8 if chained. |\n34: | 10 | **Known remote branch rewrite:** push `--force`, `-f`, leading `+`, or broad `--force-with-lease` when the resolved known destination would retreat/rewrite; explicit `<ref>:<expect>` with no rewrite evidence is silent. | Destination/source/local remote-tracking SHA and lease form are local; server comparison is execution-time and raceable. | Option/state-gated rate **unmeasured**. Named NEVER #1/ESCALATE #4; semantics **confirmed**, remote impact **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:21-21] | Critical shared-history cost; refs ~10 ms after destination resolution; overlaps ranks 11-13 and supplies primary fact. |\n35: | 11 | **Known remote deletion/batch removal:** `push --delete`, `:<dst>`, destructive `--prune`, or `--mirror` with at least one positively known destination. | Effective mappings, local known refs, and destination namespace are available; authoritative remote set is not. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. New; command semantics **confirmed**, remote impact **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:23-23] | Critical shared-ref loss; ~10 ms ref inventory; coalesce tag/multi-destination counts. |\n36: | 12 | **Known tag force/delete:** force or delete refspec resolving to `refs/tags/<tag>`, including force with `--tags`, only for a positively known existing/version tag. | Namespace/local tag type/target and known remote snapshot are local; release consumers and authoritative remote target unavailable. | Fire rate **unmeasured**; 143 current tags are exposure only. New enforcement-gap rule; gap/semantics **confirmed**, remote consequence **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:25-25] | Critical release-identity cost; ref inventory ~10 ms; suppressed into rank 10/11 with `tag` fact. |\n37: | 13 | **Destructive multi-destination push:** >1 destination where at least one is force/delete/mirror/prune, or a remote group creates sequential cross-remote publication. | Expanded local refspec/group count and `--atomic` presence are available; capability and partial outcome are not. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. New; semantics **confirmed**, prevalence **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:27-27] | High partial-publication cost; config/ref parsing; secondary `N destinations` fact under ranks 10-12. |\n38: | 14 | **Published explicit rebase:** mutating `git rebase [--onto ...] <upstream> [<branch>]`, excluding recovery/control forms, when the local rewrite set intersects positively known shared refs. | Parsed local rewrite set and local containment are available; refs can race. `pull --rebase` post-fetch set is excluded. | Broad rebase proxy 44/1,486 = **2.96%**; gated subset **unmeasured**. Named NEVER #8; local predicate **confirmed**, completeness **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:11-11] | High shared-history cost; refs/graph after exact match; overlaps rank 15 and wins. |\n39: | 15 | **Dirty autostash exposure:** mutating rebase/pull/merge form with explicit/effective autostash and nonempty tracked dirty state. | Effective config/options and dirty tracked paths are local and genuinely available; conflict/reapply outcome is not. | Option/state-gated rate **unmeasured**. Named ALWAYS #14; state/semantics **confirmed**, outcome risk **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:16-16] | High recovery cost; diff/status 68-594 ms; secondary fact under rank 14. |\n40: | 16 | **Tracked worktree overwrite:** `git restore [--worktree] [--source=...] -- <pathspec>` or legacy `git checkout [<tree>] -- <pathspec>` when selected tracked deltas are nonempty; staged-only restore excluded. | Source/index/worktree comparison for exact pathspec is local; parser fidelity required and snapshot can race. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. New; semantics **confirmed**, impact parser **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:17-17] | High local loss; diff ~68-93 ms; separate from hard reset unless chained. |\n41: | 17 | **Force-delete branch with unique commits:** `git branch -D <branch>...`/`--delete --force` for an unoccupied target with commits absent from every other durable local/remote ref. | Worktree ownership, target SHA, and all-other-ref reachability are local and available; external clones unavailable. | Invocation rate **unmeasured**; prior exposure 13 non-merged candidates among 46 branches was not fire rate. ALWAYS #17 extension; local predicate **confirmed**, external value **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:19-19] | High local-history loss; worktree/ref/graph probes; suppressed by rank 6 when part of same cleanup. |\n42: | 18 | **Selective commit mismatch:** `git commit [--only] <pathspec>...` when native dry-run shows a requested changed path absent or a nonempty staged set held back. | Parsed request, HEAD/index/worktree sets, and native pre-hook dry-run are available; operator intent/final post-hook tree are not. | Exact rate **unmeasured**; generic multi-path rate 90.6% proves count-only gating noisy. Observed incident plus official semantics; predicate **confirmed**, intent **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:17-17] | High omission cost; commit dry-run ~602-607 ms; wins staging coalescing. |\n43: | 19 | **One-sided inferred rename selection:** direct reproducible `git add ...` pathspec where exactly one side of a `diff -M` pair would change index state. | Rename heuristic, baseline index, and dry-run selection are available; semantic identity/ownership unavailable and must not be claimed. | Exact rate **unmeasured**; rename/copy appeared in 7.2% of 500 commits. Named ALWAYS #10 extension plus incident; heuristic **confirmed**, intent **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:23-23] | High split-rename cost; rename ~90 ms plus add dry-run ~438-505 ms; primary staging fact unless rank 18 matches. |\n44: | 20 | **Forced ignored staging:** `git add -f|--force <pathspec>` with a nonempty ignored candidate set; dry-run/intent/interactive forms excluded. | Reproducible dry-run selection plus `check-ignore` is local and available; contents need not be read. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. New; semantics **confirmed**, sensitivity risk **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:25-25] | High leakage/artifact cost; add dry-run ~438-505 ms; coalesce with rank 19. |\n45: | 21 | **Detached/linked push leaving another checkout stale:** push resolving to `<branch>` while source is detached/linked and another worktree has `<branch>` checked out. | Effective destination plus worktree registry/source/other HEAD are local and available; push success/follower movement unavailable. | Exact rate **unmeasured**; current exposure 1 detached of 35 worktrees and 6 tips outside primary HEAD. Named ALWAYS #15 plus incident; local consequence **confirmed**, operator surprise **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:13-13] | High coordination cost; worktree list ~16-40 ms; secondary to destructive push rules. |\n46: | 22 | **Manual wrapper publication:** direct `git push origin HEAD:$SPECKIT_LIVE_BRANCH` from linked `work/*` with `SPECKIT_AUTOSYNC=1`, excluding `git-sync.sh`. | Worktree namespace, exact environment, destination, and direct command are genuinely available. | Fire rate **unmeasured**; current predicate false. Named ALWAYS #16 extension; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:17-17] | High race/reconciliation cost; cheap local/env probes; coalesce with rank 21. |\n47: | 23 | **Positive `gh` owner/account mismatch:** `gh pr create` or `gh release create` when resolved repository owner differs from the active `gh` host account. | Repository owner and active `gh` account are available snapshots for `gh`; if cached/local identity cannot be obtained within budget, remain silent. | Mismatch rate **unmeasured**; current predicate was false. Observed 403 incident refined; identity comparison **confirmed**, authorization inference rejected. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:19-19] | Medium-high wrong-account cost; local/cached probe latency unmeasured, network forbidden in hot path; never merge into a claim that push will fail. |\n48: \n49: ## Explicitly Rejected Candidate Matrix\n50: \n51: | Rejected candidate / exact operation | Pre-state and availability | Noise / source / confidence | Rejection |\n52: |---|---|---|---|\n53: | Every `git commit`, `reset`, `rebase`, `pull`, or `push`. | Exact hazardous option/state is absent from the broad shape. | Commit 73.55%, reset 13.53%, rebase 2.96%; source: history proxy; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:34-38] | Expected noise exceeds aggregate ceiling; use retained exact predicates. |\n54: | `git commit -a|--all` when the only positive fact is a nonempty tracked dirty set/shared primary tree. | Dirty set is available; cross-session ownership and accidental intent are unavailable. | Exact option rate **unmeasured**; 57.4% of commits touched 10+ paths; source: new extension; semantics **confirmed**, contamination **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:15-15] | Expected count-based noise is too high and the hazardous predicate is unavailable. |\n55: | `git add -A|--all`, `git add .`, or `git add <directory>` based only on count, top-level spread, or a pre-existing index. | Candidate sets are available; ownership/accident is unavailable. | Exact rate **unmeasured**; 90.6% multi-path and 9.2% cross-root history; named scoped-staging rule plus incident; set facts **confirmed**, intent **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:13-13] | Retain only ranks 19-20 concrete mismatches; generic broad-add noise cannot be bounded. |\n56: | `git commit --include <paths>` unconditionally. | Staged/selected sets are available; conflict-completion intent is not, and the option explicitly adds to the index. | Rate **unmeasured**; new; semantics **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:19-19] | Explicit routine recovery mode; no distinct positive hazard. |\n57: | `git add -p|-i|-e`, `git commit -p`, or `--pathspec-from-file=-` based on predicted selection. | Final interactive/stdin selection does not exist before execution. | Rate **unmeasured**; new boundary; **confirmed** unavailable. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:21-21] | Exact state predicate unavailable. |\n58: | Published-history warning for `git pull --rebase` based on the pre-fetch rewrite set. | Existing refs/config are available; the command's fetch changes the authoritative upstream after PreToolUse. | Broad rebase 2.96%; exact subset **unmeasured**; named rules; **confirmed** boundary. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:11-11] | Exact rewrite predicate unavailable; retain only dirty/autostash rank 15. |\n59: | Generic `filter-branch`/`filter-repo` umbrella, including help/analyze/dry forms. | Tool-specific mutating form and affected ref set were not validated across variants. | Rate **unmeasured**; new candidate; **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:30-32] | Exact mutating predicate unavailable in this evidence set; do not ship a name-only warning. |\n60: | Ordinary `git branch -d`, or `branch -D` targeting a branch checked out elsewhere. | Merge/worktree ownership is available, but Git refuses these unsafe forms at execution. | Rate **unmeasured**; Git/sk-git protection **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:19-19] | Protection already enforced; only rank 17's unoccupied unique-commit case remains. |\n61: | Ordinary `git worktree remove <path>` or `git worktree prune`. | Registration/cleanliness is available; Git/reaper already protects dirty/live lanes. | Rate **unmeasured**; named ALWAYS #17; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:21-21] | Protection/routine cleanup already owns it. |\n62: | `git clean` without force, every clean/prune dry-run, staged-only `restore`, rebase `--abort|--continue|--skip|--quit`, `stash apply`, conflicted `stash pop`, default reflog expiry, or routine `git gc`. | Safety/recovery mode is exactly command-visible; state may be available but loss predicate is absent or Git preserves the recovery object. | Rates **unmeasured**; installed Git/sk-git sources; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:36-44] | Existing protection or routine recovery makes an advisory redundant/noisy. |\n63: | Non-allowlisted branch permission, wrapper-branch publication, or branch-name grammar on `git push`. | Destination/allowlist is local; pre-push receives final ref input and owns the block. | Block rate **unmeasured**; named remote policy; **confirmed**, despite current missing installed hook. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:29-37] | Already enforcement-owned; installation health is a separate control. |\n64: | `git push` account-owner mismatch used to predict 403, authorization, protection, or success. | `gh` identity/API permission may be read, but Git's actual HTTPS/SSH credential and receive-time policy are unavailable. | Mismatch/failure rates **unmeasured**; incident refinement; boundary **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:19-19] | Exact transport/outcome predicate unavailable; retain rank 23 only for direct `gh`. |\n65: | Ordinary first-time tag publication or nondestructive multi-ref push. | Destinations are available; no positive destructive state exists. | Rates **unmeasured**; new candidates; semantics **confirmed**, expected noise **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:39-45] | No high-cost predicate; generic multi-ref/tag messages would spend attention without protection. |\n66: | Treating absent remote containment, successful API/`ls-remote`, lease snapshot, or pre-hook commit candidate as a guarantee. | Each is only a current snapshot; remote receive, hooks, concurrent writers, and final object are later. | Not an invocation-rate candidate; source boundary **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:47-57] | Required state is unavailable or raceable; absence must remain unknown. |\n67: \n68: ## Probe and Alert Budgets\n69: \n70: 1. **Stage 0, command-only:** parse direct `git`/`git -C`/eligible `gh`; no subprocess for nonmatches. Exact help, dry-run, recovery, and safer forms are rejected here. [INFERENCE: based on the cheap-probe ordering in iteration 2]\n71: 2. **Normal state tier:** at most 3 Git subprocesses, reused across matching rules; target `<=100 ms` observed p95 for ref/worktree/diff checks and hard timeout `250 ms`. On timeout/error, remain silent rather than inventing state. [SOURCE: bounded read-only Git benchmark captured 2026-07-27T19:41:12Z]\n72: 3. **Rare mutation tier:** after an exact destructive/selective token, at most 5 subprocesses and `750 ms` total; this admits current status/add/commit dry-runs. No network and no all-worktree sweep. [SOURCE: bounded read-only Git benchmark captured 2026-07-27T19:41:12Z]\n73: 4. **Exceptional clean-ignored tier:** exact `clean -fx|-fdx` may use its native dry-run with a `3.5 s` hard cap because the measured maximum was 3.25 s; record latency telemetry and disable/retune if p95 remains above 2 s. [SOURCE: bounded read-only Git benchmark captured 2026-07-27T19:41:12Z]\n74: 5. **Alert telemetry:** record only normalized rule id, eligible operation class, predicate matched, emitted/coalesced flag, latency bucket, and timeout—never raw command, paths, refs, URLs, or credentials. Evaluate rates per 100 direct eligible Git invocations. [INFERENCE: this is the minimum data needed to replace unavailable argv/fire-rate history without collecting command content]\n75: \n76: ## Ruled Out\n77: \n78: - Broad operation-family and path-count warnings: measured history proxies exceed the attention budget or fail to prove a hazard.\n79: - Any predicate that calls absent remote containment “safe,” predicts post-fetch/post-hook state, or maps `gh` identity to Git transport authorization.\n80: - Duplicate branch naming/permission advisories already owned by pre-push enforcement.\n81: - Network checks, full object scans, and all-worktree status sweeps in the synchronous hot path.\n82: \n83: ## Dead Ends\n84: \n85: - Exact option-sensitive historical fire rates cannot be reconstructed from Git log/reflog. This is now final negative knowledge, not a remaining research task; only future normalized PreToolUse telemetry can measure the retained matrix. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md:44-49]\n86: - Session ownership is not encoded in Git state. Generic broad staging and `commit -a` cannot be made precise by another path-count or top-level heuristic. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:44-47]\n87: \n88: ## Edge Cases\n89: \n90: - Ambiguous input: “cost” could mean failure cost or synchronous probe cost; the matrix reports both so ranking remains auditable.\n91: - Contradictory evidence: tracked pre-push enforcement owns naming/permission while the current installed path lacks the hook. The decision remains to reject duplicate advisories and repair hook health separately. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:29-37]\n92: - Missing dependencies: normalized PreToolUse invocation/match telemetry does not exist, so every option-sensitive fire rate is explicitly unmeasured; history proxies and current exposure are not relabeled as fire rates.\n93: - Partial success: none. The remaining noise question is answered as an enforceable target plus shadow-measurement gate, without inventing historical option rates.\n94: \n95: ## Sources Consulted\n96: \n97: - `research/BRIEFING.md:1-59`\n98: - `research/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json:1-50`\n99: - `research/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl:1-5`\n100: - `research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md:1-108`\n101: - `research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json:1-110`\n102: - `research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:1-91`\n103: - `research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:1-82`\n104: - `research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:1-83`\n105: - `research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:1-88`\n106: - `research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-001.jsonl` through `iter-004.jsonl`\n107: - Bounded read-only Git latency and exposure measurements captured 2026-07-27T19:41:12Z; no fetch, push, ref mutation, staging, commit, checkout, or file write was performed by the probes.\n108: \n109: ## Assessment\n110: \n111: - New information ratio: 0.80 (`2` fully new findings, `3` partially new synthesis findings: `(2 + 0.5*3)/5 = 0.70`, plus `0.10` simplicity bonus for resolving the final open question and reducing candidates to a deployable model).\n112: - Questions addressed: final candidate ranking; exact negative knowledge; measured probe latency; one-line coalescing; per-rule and aggregate noise targets.\n113: - Questions answered: how often can candidates legitimately be measured from existing history, where the defensible noise threshold sits, and which complete rule set should advance to shadow calibration.\n114: \n115: ## Reflection\n116: \n117: - What worked and why: reusing exact prior candidate evidence while benchmarking only the missing latency dimension avoided repeating the exhausted history search and made probe cost comparable across rule families.\n118: - What did not work and why: repository history still cannot recover option-sensitive commands, failures, or state-predicate matches because those data were never recorded.\n119: - What I would do differently: run the retained classifier in privacy-preserving shadow mode until each rule and aggregate denominator meets the stated sample gate; promote only rules below their ceilings, except explicit bypass/immediate-destruction rules which should trigger workflow review if unexpectedly frequent.\n120: \n121: ## Recommended Next Focus\n122: \n123: Stop this lineage at max iteration 5. The next phase should translate the 23 retained rows into a shadow-mode rule specification, benchmark the exact implementation against the stated latency caps, and promote only after normalized telemetry validates the per-rule and aggregate alert ceilings.\n\n(End of file - total 123 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Iteration 5: Final Candidate Matrix and Noise Threshold\n\n## Canonical Route Proof\n\n`Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research`; `agent_definition_loaded=true`; detached lineage `sol`; forced run/iteration `5 of 5`; `stopPolicy=max-iterations`; LEAF execution with no sub-agent dispatch.\n\n## Focus\n\nCalibrate every candidate retained through iterations 1-4 into a decision-ready advisory rule set. Ranking uses four explicit dimensions: positive-evidence strength (`E3` exact command plus positive local state, `E2` exact command-only destructive/policy intent, `E1` raceable or heuristic positive snapshot), cost of the failure, overlap with a higher-ranked rule, and measured prevalence where Git history legitimately exposes it. Option-sensitive fire rates remain unmeasured because Git history contains ref outcomes, not complete argv, failed commands, or preflight-state matches. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md:44-58] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/BRIEFING.md:38-59]\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **The final retained set is 23 narrowly gated rules, not broad Git-family warnings.** Each row below supplies the exact operation, genuinely available pre-state, measured or explicitly unmeasured noise, source classification, confidence, harm cost, measured/expected probe cost, and coalescing overlap. [INFERENCE: based on the candidate validations in iterations 1-4 and the ranking criteria stated above]\n2. **Fourteen candidate classes are rejected for unavailable predicates, existing protection, or excessive expected noise.** In particular, session ownership, post-fetch rewrite sets, Git transport identity, remote authorization, final push/commit outcomes, and interactive/stdin selections are not genuine pre-execution facts. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:31-47] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:33-50]\n3. **Probe latency requires a tiered budget.** Five-run medians/maxima in the current checkout were: `rev-parse` 7.87/26.84 ms, ref inventory 10.15/13.71 ms, `--contains=HEAD` 15.71/36.59 ms, worktree list 15.72/39.68 ms, stash list 16.22/23.94 ms, diff 68.27/92.32 ms, rename diff 89.73/92.93 ms, reflog-expire dry-run 148.21/149.99 ms, clean dry-run 336.28/425.09 ms, add dry-run 438.31/505.34 ms, status 464.68/593.83 ms, commit dry-run 601.58/606.63 ms, and `clean -ndx` 1,630.21/3,254.80 ms. A 35-worktree status sweep took 20,147.45 ms and is rejected from the hot path. [SOURCE: bounded read-only Git benchmark captured 2026-07-27T19:41:12Z]\n4. **The attention budget is measurable only with future normalized PreToolUse telemetry, so rollout must begin in shadow mode.** Target `<0.5` emitted alerts per 100 direct Git invocations per rule, hard ceiling `1/100`; target `<2/100` aggregate, hard ceiling `3/100`, after one-line coalescing and a minimum 500 eligible invocations or 30 days. These are design targets, not observed rates. The repository proxy shows why: amend outcomes were 0.47%, rebase 2.96%, reset 13.53%, and commit 73.55%; 90.6% of 500 commits were multi-path. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:9-17] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:13-29] [INFERENCE: broad-family rates above the aggregate budget require positive state gates]\n5. **One-line coalescing is the release contract, not a presentation preference.** Emit at most one line for the whole Bash invocation, at most two positive facts plus `+N`, in priority order `irrecoverable local loss > shared/remote rewrite > selection mismatch > coordination`; reuse probe results and suppress lower-ranked overlaps and enforcement-owned messages. Format: `Advisory: <operation> — <primary fact>; <secondary fact>[; +N].` Cap at 180 characters and never print raw URLs, credentials, or file contents. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/BRIEFING.md:52-59] [INFERENCE: one line and priority suppression keep aggregate attention cost bounded when one command matches several predicates]\n\n## Retained Candidate Matrix (ranked)\n","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-005.md","text":"# Iteration 5: Final Candidate Matrix and Noise Threshold\n\n## Canonical Route Proof\n\n`Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research`; `agent_definition_loaded=true`; detached lineage `sol`; forced run/iteration `5 of 5`; `stopPolicy=max-iterations`; LEAF execution with no sub-agent dispatch.\n\n## Focus\n\nCalibrate every candidate retained through iterations 1-4 into a decision-ready advisory rule set. Ranking uses four explicit dimensions: positive-evidence strength (`E3` exact command plus positive local state, `E2` exact command-only destructive/policy intent, `E1` raceable or heuristic positive snapshot), cost of the failure, overlap with a higher-ranked rule, and measured prevalence where Git history legitimately exposes it. Option-sensitive fire rates remain unmeasured because Git history contains ref outcomes, not complete argv, failed commands, or preflight-state matches. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md:44-58] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/BRIEFING.md:38-59]\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **The final retained set is 23 narrowly gated rules, not broad Git-family warnings.** Each row below supplies the exact operation, genuinely available pre-state, measured or explicitly unmeasured noise, source classification, confidence, harm cost, measured/expected probe cost, and coalescing overlap. [INFERENCE: based on the candidate validations in iterations 1-4 and the ranking criteria stated above]\n2. **Fourteen candidate classes are rejected for unavailable predicates, existing protection, or excessive expected noise.** In particular, session ownership, post-fetch rewrite sets, Git transport identity, remote authorization, final push/commit outcomes, and interactive/stdin selections are not genuine pre-execution facts. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:31-47] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:33-50]\n3. **Probe latency requires a tiered budget.** Five-run medians/maxima in the current checkout were: `rev-parse` 7.87/26.84 ms, ref inventory 10.15/13.71 ms, `--contains=HEAD` 15.71/36.59 ms, worktree list 15.72/39.68 ms, stash list 16.22/23.94 ms, diff 68.27/92.32 ms, rename diff 89.73/92.93 ms, reflog-expire dry-run 148.21/149.99 ms, clean dry-run 336.28/425.09 ms, add dry-run 438.31/505.34 ms, status 464.68/593.83 ms, commit dry-run 601.58/606.63 ms, and `clean -ndx` 1,630.21/3,254.80 ms. A 35-worktree status sweep took 20,147.45 ms and is rejected from the hot path. [SOURCE: bounded read-only Git benchmark captured 2026-07-27T19:41:12Z]\n4. **The attention budget is measurable only with future normalized PreToolUse telemetry, so rollout must begin in shadow mode.** Target `<0.5` emitted alerts per 100 direct Git invocations per rule, hard ceiling `1/100`; target `<2/100` aggregate, hard ceiling `3/100`, after one-line coalescing and a minimum 500 eligible invocations or 30 days. These are design targets, not observed rates. The repository proxy shows why: amend outcomes were 0.47%, rebase 2.96%, reset 13.53%, and commit 73.55%; 90.6% of 500 commits were multi-path. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:9-17] [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:13-29] [INFERENCE: broad-family rates above the aggregate budget require positive state gates]\n5. **One-line coalescing is the release contract, not a presentation preference.** Emit at most one line for the whole Bash invocation, at most two positive facts plus `+N`, in priority order `irrecoverable local loss > shared/remote rewrite > selection mismatch > coordination`; reuse probe results and suppress lower-ranked overlaps and enforcement-owned messages. Format: `Advisory: <operation> — <primary fact>; <secondary fact>[; +N].` Cap at 180 characters and never print raw URLs, credentials, or file contents. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/BRIEFING.md:52-59] [INFERENCE: one line and priority suppression keep aggregate attention cost bounded when one command matches several predicates]\n\n## Retained Candidate Matrix (ranked)\n\nThe rows absorb every retained candidate from iterations 1-4; variants are grouped only when they share the same predicate and remediation.\n\n| Rank | Candidate and exact operation | Pre-state and genuine availability | Noise / source / confidence | Cost, probe, overlap |\n|---:|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | **Hook bypass:** direct `git commit ... --no-verify` or `git push ... --no-verify`. | Exact parsed option; command-only and genuinely available for direct Git. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. Named sk-git NEVER #9; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:10-12] | Critical because it removes enforcement; zero Git probes; coalesce with any lower rule but never suppress. |\n| 2 | **Direct branch creation:** `git branch <new>`, `checkout -b|-B`, or `switch -c|-C`. | Exact direct command; optional branch/worktree existence is local. Opaque aliases/scripts unavailable. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. Named NEVER #2; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:10-10] | High process/collision cost; command-only or ~16 ms worktree probe; no enforcement overlap found. |\n| 3 | **Published amend:** `git commit ... --amend`. | Positive containment of `HEAD` by a remote-tracking or integration ref is local and available; absence never proves unpublished. | Broad amend proxy 7/1,486 = **0.47%**; gated subset **unmeasured**. Named NEVER #10; local predicate **confirmed**, publication completeness **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:9-9] | Critical shared-history rewrite; ~16 ms containment; overlaps path/`-a` amend and wins coalescing. |\n| 4 | **Hard reset with positive loss:** `git reset --hard [<target>]`. | Exact target plus nonempty index/worktree overwrite or positive branch-tip retreat relative to other durable refs; locally available snapshot. | Broad reset proxy 201/1,486 = **13.53%**; hard/state-gated rate **unmeasured**. New extension of ALWAYS #15; predicate **confirmed**, durable-ref valuation **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:13-13] | Critical local loss; diff ~68 ms plus refs ~10 ms; wins over generic restore/history-loss facts. |\n| 5 | **Forced clean with actual removals:** `git clean -f|-ff` preserving `-d`, `-x|-X`, exclusions, and pathspec; exclude dry-run. | Native equivalent `git clean -n...` returns at least one removal; exact selection is genuinely available but raceable. | Invocation/fire rate **unmeasured**. New; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:15-15] | Critical untracked/ignored loss; 336-425 ms normally, `-x` 1.63-3.25 s exceptional tier; coalesce removal count only. |\n| 6 | **Forced removal of a dirty/live worktree:** `git worktree remove -f|--force <path>`. | Exact target registration/status and positive live wrapper PID; local and available. Missing marker is unknown, not inactive. | Invocation rate **unmeasured**; current exposure 20 dirty of 35 worktrees. Named ALWAYS #17; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:21-21] | Critical local/session loss; inspect only target, never 20.15 s all-worktree sweep; overlaps branch deletion and wins. |\n| 7 | **Unrescued stash destruction:** `git stash drop [<stash>]` or `git stash clear`. | Resolve selected SHA(s), rescue/durable refs, and count entries lacking rescue; local and available, selector race acknowledged. | Invocation rate **unmeasured**; current exposure 20 stash entries, none directly rescued. ALWAYS #14 extension; availability **confirmed**, durable suppression **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:23-23] | Critical recovery loss; stash/ref probes ~16/10 ms; coalesce with expiry/prune as one recovery warning. |\n| 8 | **Immediate reflog expiry with nonempty dry-run:** `git reflog expire --expire=now|--expire-unreachable=now ...`; exclude `--dry-run`. | Native `--dry-run --verbose` for selected refs; local snapshot genuinely available. | Invocation rate **unmeasured**; 390 reflog-only commits were an exposure count, not fire rate. New; **confirmed** for dry-run, importance **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:25-25] | Critical recovery-pointer loss; ~148-150 ms; coalesce with immediate prune. |\n| 9 | **Immediate object pruning:** `git gc --prune=now`, effective `gc.pruneExpire=now`, or `git prune --expire=now`; exclude dry-run/routine forms. | Exact token/effective config is genuinely available; exact future deletion set and concurrent-writer safety are not required or claimable. | Invocation rate **unmeasured**; prior 87,410 unreachable objects is exposure only. New; command/config **confirmed**, consequence set **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:27-27] | Critical recovery-window collapse; command/config only—do not run `fsck`/full reachability; suppressed into rank 8 if chained. |\n| 10 | **Known remote branch rewrite:** push `--force`, `-f`, leading `+`, or broad `--force-with-lease` when the resolved known destination would retreat/rewrite; explicit `<ref>:<expect>` with no rewrite evidence is silent. | Destination/source/local remote-tracking SHA and lease form are local; server comparison is execution-time and raceable. | Option/state-gated rate **unmeasured**. Named NEVER #1/ESCALATE #4; semantics **confirmed**, remote impact **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:21-21] | Critical shared-history cost; refs ~10 ms after destination resolution; overlaps ranks 11-13 and supplies primary fact. |\n| 11 | **Known remote deletion/batch removal:** `push --delete`, `:<dst>`, destructive `--prune`, or `--mirror` with at least one positively known destination. | Effective mappings, local known refs, and destination namespace are available; authoritative remote set is not. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. New; command semantics **confirmed**, remote impact **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:23-23] | Critical shared-ref loss; ~10 ms ref inventory; coalesce tag/multi-destination counts. |\n| 12 | **Known tag force/delete:** force or delete refspec resolving to `refs/tags/<tag>`, including force with `--tags`, only for a positively known existing/version tag. | Namespace/local tag type/target and known remote snapshot are local; release consumers and authoritative remote target unavailable. | Fire rate **unmeasured**; 143 current tags are exposure only. New enforcement-gap rule; gap/semantics **confirmed**, remote consequence **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:25-25] | Critical release-identity cost; ref inventory ~10 ms; suppressed into rank 10/11 with `tag` fact. |\n| 13 | **Destructive multi-destination push:** >1 destination where at least one is force/delete/mirror/prune, or a remote group creates sequential cross-remote publication. | Expanded local refspec/group count and `--atomic` presence are available; capability and partial outcome are not. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. New; semantics **confirmed**, prevalence **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:27-27] | High partial-publication cost; config/ref parsing; secondary `N destinations` fact under ranks 10-12. |\n| 14 | **Published explicit rebase:** mutating `git rebase [--onto ...] <upstream> [<branch>]`, excluding recovery/control forms, when the local rewrite set intersects positively known shared refs. | Parsed local rewrite set and local containment are available; refs can race. `pull --rebase` post-fetch set is excluded. | Broad rebase proxy 44/1,486 = **2.96%**; gated subset **unmeasured**. Named NEVER #8; local predicate **confirmed**, completeness **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:11-11] | High shared-history cost; refs/graph after exact match; overlaps rank 15 and wins. |\n| 15 | **Dirty autostash exposure:** mutating rebase/pull/merge form with explicit/effective autostash and nonempty tracked dirty state. | Effective config/options and dirty tracked paths are local and genuinely available; conflict/reapply outcome is not. | Option/state-gated rate **unmeasured**. Named ALWAYS #14; state/semantics **confirmed**, outcome risk **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:16-16] | High recovery cost; diff/status 68-594 ms; secondary fact under rank 14. |\n| 16 | **Tracked worktree overwrite:** `git restore [--worktree] [--source=...] -- <pathspec>` or legacy `git checkout [<tree>] -- <pathspec>` when selected tracked deltas are nonempty; staged-only restore excluded. | Source/index/worktree comparison for exact pathspec is local; parser fidelity required and snapshot can race. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. New; semantics **confirmed**, impact parser **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:17-17] | High local loss; diff ~68-93 ms; separate from hard reset unless chained. |\n| 17 | **Force-delete branch with unique commits:** `git branch -D <branch>...`/`--delete --force` for an unoccupied target with commits absent from every other durable local/remote ref. | Worktree ownership, target SHA, and all-other-ref reachability are local and available; external clones unavailable. | Invocation rate **unmeasured**; prior exposure 13 non-merged candidates among 46 branches was not fire rate. ALWAYS #17 extension; local predicate **confirmed**, external value **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:19-19] | High local-history loss; worktree/ref/graph probes; suppressed by rank 6 when part of same cleanup. |\n| 18 | **Selective commit mismatch:** `git commit [--only] <pathspec>...` when native dry-run shows a requested changed path absent or a nonempty staged set held back. | Parsed request, HEAD/index/worktree sets, and native pre-hook dry-run are available; operator intent/final post-hook tree are not. | Exact rate **unmeasured**; generic multi-path rate 90.6% proves count-only gating noisy. Observed incident plus official semantics; predicate **confirmed**, intent **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:17-17] | High omission cost; commit dry-run ~602-607 ms; wins staging coalescing. |\n| 19 | **One-sided inferred rename selection:** direct reproducible `git add ...` pathspec where exactly one side of a `diff -M` pair would change index state. | Rename heuristic, baseline index, and dry-run selection are available; semantic identity/ownership unavailable and must not be claimed. | Exact rate **unmeasured**; rename/copy appeared in 7.2% of 500 commits. Named ALWAYS #10 extension plus incident; heuristic **confirmed**, intent **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:23-23] | High split-rename cost; rename ~90 ms plus add dry-run ~438-505 ms; primary staging fact unless rank 18 matches. |\n| 20 | **Forced ignored staging:** `git add -f|--force <pathspec>` with a nonempty ignored candidate set; dry-run/intent/interactive forms excluded. | Reproducible dry-run selection plus `check-ignore` is local and available; contents need not be read. | Fire rate **unmeasured**. New; semantics **confirmed**, sensitivity risk **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:25-25] | High leakage/artifact cost; add dry-run ~438-505 ms; coalesce with rank 19. |\n| 21 | **Detached/linked push leaving another checkout stale:** push resolving to `<branch>` while source is detached/linked and another worktree has `<branch>` checked out. | Effective destination plus worktree registry/source/other HEAD are local and available; push success/follower movement unavailable. | Exact rate **unmeasured**; current exposure 1 detached of 35 worktrees and 6 tips outside primary HEAD. Named ALWAYS #15 plus incident; local consequence **confirmed**, operator surprise **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:13-13] | High coordination cost; worktree list ~16-40 ms; secondary to destructive push rules. |\n| 22 | **Manual wrapper publication:** direct `git push origin HEAD:$SPECKIT_LIVE_BRANCH` from linked `work/*` with `SPECKIT_AUTOSYNC=1`, excluding `git-sync.sh`. | Worktree namespace, exact environment, destination, and direct command are genuinely available. | Fire rate **unmeasured**; current predicate false. Named ALWAYS #16 extension; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:17-17] | High race/reconciliation cost; cheap local/env probes; coalesce with rank 21. |\n| 23 | **Positive `gh` owner/account mismatch:** `gh pr create` or `gh release create` when resolved repository owner differs from the active `gh` host account. | Repository owner and active `gh` account are available snapshots for `gh`; if cached/local identity cannot be obtained within budget, remain silent. | Mismatch rate **unmeasured**; current predicate was false. Observed 403 incident refined; identity comparison **confirmed**, authorization inference rejected. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:19-19] | Medium-high wrong-account cost; local/cached probe latency unmeasured, network forbidden in hot path; never merge into a claim that push will fail. |\n\n## Explicitly Rejected Candidate Matrix\n\n| Rejected candidate / exact operation | Pre-state and availability | Noise / source / confidence | Rejection |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Every `git commit`, `reset`, `rebase`, `pull`, or `push`. | Exact hazardous option/state is absent from the broad shape. | Commit 73.55%, reset 13.53%, rebase 2.96%; source: history proxy; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:34-38] | Expected noise exceeds aggregate ceiling; use retained exact predicates. |\n| `git commit -a|--all` when the only positive fact is a nonempty tracked dirty set/shared primary tree. | Dirty set is available; cross-session ownership and accidental intent are unavailable. | Exact option rate **unmeasured**; 57.4% of commits touched 10+ paths; source: new extension; semantics **confirmed**, contamination **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:15-15] | Expected count-based noise is too high and the hazardous predicate is unavailable. |\n| `git add -A|--all`, `git add .`, or `git add <directory>` based only on count, top-level spread, or a pre-existing index. | Candidate sets are available; ownership/accident is unavailable. | Exact rate **unmeasured**; 90.6% multi-path and 9.2% cross-root history; named scoped-staging rule plus incident; set facts **confirmed**, intent **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:13-13] | Retain only ranks 19-20 concrete mismatches; generic broad-add noise cannot be bounded. |\n| `git commit --include <paths>` unconditionally. | Staged/selected sets are available; conflict-completion intent is not, and the option explicitly adds to the index. | Rate **unmeasured**; new; semantics **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:19-19] | Explicit routine recovery mode; no distinct positive hazard. |\n| `git add -p|-i|-e`, `git commit -p`, or `--pathspec-from-file=-` based on predicted selection. | Final interactive/stdin selection does not exist before execution. | Rate **unmeasured**; new boundary; **confirmed** unavailable. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:21-21] | Exact state predicate unavailable. |\n| Published-history warning for `git pull --rebase` based on the pre-fetch rewrite set. | Existing refs/config are available; the command's fetch changes the authoritative upstream after PreToolUse. | Broad rebase 2.96%; exact subset **unmeasured**; named rules; **confirmed** boundary. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:11-11] | Exact rewrite predicate unavailable; retain only dirty/autostash rank 15. |\n| Generic `filter-branch`/`filter-repo` umbrella, including help/analyze/dry forms. | Tool-specific mutating form and affected ref set were not validated across variants. | Rate **unmeasured**; new candidate; **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:30-32] | Exact mutating predicate unavailable in this evidence set; do not ship a name-only warning. |\n| Ordinary `git branch -d`, or `branch -D` targeting a branch checked out elsewhere. | Merge/worktree ownership is available, but Git refuses these unsafe forms at execution. | Rate **unmeasured**; Git/sk-git protection **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:19-19] | Protection already enforced; only rank 17's unoccupied unique-commit case remains. |\n| Ordinary `git worktree remove <path>` or `git worktree prune`. | Registration/cleanliness is available; Git/reaper already protects dirty/live lanes. | Rate **unmeasured**; named ALWAYS #17; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:21-21] | Protection/routine cleanup already owns it. |\n| `git clean` without force, every clean/prune dry-run, staged-only `restore`, rebase `--abort|--continue|--skip|--quit`, `stash apply`, conflicted `stash pop`, default reflog expiry, or routine `git gc`. | Safety/recovery mode is exactly command-visible; state may be available but loss predicate is absent or Git preserves the recovery object. | Rates **unmeasured**; installed Git/sk-git sources; **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:36-44] | Existing protection or routine recovery makes an advisory redundant/noisy. |\n| Non-allowlisted branch permission, wrapper-branch publication, or branch-name grammar on `git push`. | Destination/allowlist is local; pre-push receives final ref input and owns the block. | Block rate **unmeasured**; named remote policy; **confirmed**, despite current missing installed hook. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:29-37] | Already enforcement-owned; installation health is a separate control. |\n| `git push` account-owner mismatch used to predict 403, authorization, protection, or success. | `gh` identity/API permission may be read, but Git's actual HTTPS/SSH credential and receive-time policy are unavailable. | Mismatch/failure rates **unmeasured**; incident refinement; boundary **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:19-19] | Exact transport/outcome predicate unavailable; retain rank 23 only for direct `gh`. |\n| Ordinary first-time tag publication or nondestructive multi-ref push. | Destinations are available; no positive destructive state exists. | Rates **unmeasured**; new candidates; semantics **confirmed**, expected noise **inferred**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:39-45] | No high-cost predicate; generic multi-ref/tag messages would spend attention without protection. |\n| Treating absent remote containment, successful API/`ls-remote`, lease snapshot, or pre-hook commit candidate as a guarantee. | Each is only a current snapshot; remote receive, hooks, concurrent writers, and final object are later. | Not an invocation-rate candidate; source boundary **confirmed**. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:47-57] | Required state is unavailable or raceable; absence must remain unknown. |\n\n## Probe and Alert Budgets\n\n1. **Stage 0, command-only:** parse direct `git`/`git -C`/eligible `gh`; no subprocess for nonmatches. Exact help, dry-run, recovery, and safer forms are rejected here. [INFERENCE: based on the cheap-probe ordering in iteration 2]\n2. **Normal state tier:** at most 3 Git subprocesses, reused across matching rules; target `<=100 ms` observed p95 for ref/worktree/diff checks and hard timeout `250 ms`. On timeout/error, remain silent rather than inventing state. [SOURCE: bounded read-only Git benchmark captured 2026-07-27T19:41:12Z]\n3. **Rare mutation tier:** after an exact destructive/selective token, at most 5 subprocesses and `750 ms` total; this admits current status/add/commit dry-runs. No network and no all-worktree sweep. [SOURCE: bounded read-only Git benchmark captured 2026-07-27T19:41:12Z]\n4. **Exceptional clean-ignored tier:** exact `clean -fx|-fdx` may use its native dry-run with a `3.5 s` hard cap because the measured maximum was 3.25 s; record latency telemetry and disable/retune if p95 remains above 2 s. [SOURCE: bounded read-only Git benchmark captured 2026-07-27T19:41:12Z]\n5. **Alert telemetry:** record only normalized rule id, eligible operation class, predicate matched, emitted/coalesced flag, latency bucket, and timeout—never raw command, paths, refs, URLs, or credentials. Evaluate rates per 100 direct eligible Git invocations. [INFERENCE: this is the minimum data needed to replace unavailable argv/fire-rate history without collecting command content]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Broad operation-family and path-count warnings: measured history proxies exceed the attention budget or fail to prove a hazard.\n- Any predicate that calls absent remote containment “safe,” predicts post-fetch/post-hook state, or maps `gh` identity to Git transport authorization.\n- Duplicate branch naming/permission advisories already owned by pre-push enforcement.\n- Network checks, full object scans, and all-worktree status sweeps in the synchronous hot path.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- Exact option-sensitive historical fire rates cannot be reconstructed from Git log/reflog. This is now final negative knowledge, not a remaining research task; only future normalized PreToolUse telemetry can measure the retained matrix. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md:44-49]\n- Session ownership is not encoded in Git state. Generic broad staging and `commit -a` cannot be made precise by another path-count or top-level heuristic. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:44-47]\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: “cost” could mean failure cost or synchronous probe cost; the matrix reports both so ranking remains auditable.\n- Contradictory evidence: tracked pre-push enforcement owns naming/permission while the current installed path lacks the hook. The decision remains to reject duplicate advisories and repair hook health separately. [SOURCE: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:29-37]\n- Missing dependencies: normalized PreToolUse invocation/match telemetry does not exist, so every option-sensitive fire rate is explicitly unmeasured; history proxies and current exposure are not relabeled as fire rates.\n- Partial success: none. The remaining noise question is answered as an enforceable target plus shadow-measurement gate, without inventing historical option rates.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- `research/BRIEFING.md:1-59`\n- `research/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json:1-50`\n- `research/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl:1-5`\n- `research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md:1-108`\n- `research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json:1-110`\n- `research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md:1-91`\n- `research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md:1-82`\n- `research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md:1-83`\n- `research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md:1-88`\n- `research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-001.jsonl` through `iter-004.jsonl`\n- Bounded read-only Git latency and exposure measurements captured 2026-07-27T19:41:12Z; no fetch, push, ref mutation, staging, commit, checkout, or file write was performed by the probes.\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.80 (`2` fully new findings, `3` partially new synthesis findings: `(2 + 0.5*3)/5 = 0.70`, plus `0.10` simplicity bonus for resolving the final open question and reducing candidates to a deployable model).\n- Questions addressed: final candidate ranking; exact negative knowledge; measured probe latency; one-line coalescing; per-rule and aggregate noise targets.\n- Questions answered: how often can candidates legitimately be measured from existing history, where the defensible noise threshold sits, and which complete rule set should advance to shadow calibration.\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: reusing exact prior candidate evidence while benchmarking only the missing latency dimension avoided repeating the exhausted history search and made probe cost comparable across rule families.\n- What did not work and why: repository history still cannot recover option-sensitive commands, failures, or state-predicate matches because those data were never recorded.\n- What I would do differently: run the retained classifier in privacy-preserving shadow mode until each rule and aggregate denominator meets the stated sample gate; promote only rules below their ceilings, except explicit bypass/immediate-destruction rules which should trigger workflow review if unexpectedly frequent.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nStop this lineage at max iteration 5. The next phase should translate the 23 retained rows into a shadow-mode rule specification, benchmark the exact implementation against the stated latency caps, and promote only after normalized telemetry validates the per-rule and aggregate alert ceilings.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":123,"totalLines":123,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-005.md","time":{"start":1785181558071,"end":1785181558089}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0e9d49173a304904016a67b575f16081918197cb850956d165"}},"id":"prt_fa51cd4f0001gB1yv4zE0tGelm","sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","messageID":"msg_fa51cb35f001y9TxP92s850RPv"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785181558100,"sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_Azm9CF9GP05FFpftO5r39uMr","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-005.jsonl"},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-005.jsonl</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":5,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":5,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Calibrate the final candidate matrix and noise threshold into a decision-ready rule set\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.8,\"noveltyJustification\":\"2 of 5 findings were fully new and 3 partially new, yielding 0.70 plus a 0.10 simplicity bonus for resolving the final open question.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"How often would each candidate fire in real repository history, and what is the defensible noise threshold?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"How often can retained candidates legitimately be measured from existing history, where should the noise threshold sit, and what final ranked rule set should advance?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Broad Git-family, path-count, and ownership-inference warnings\",\"Predicates requiring post-fetch, post-hook, transport-credential, authorization, or final remote outcome state\",\"Duplicate naming and permission advisories already owned by pre-push enforcement\",\"Network probes, full object scans, and all-worktree sweeps in the synchronous hot path\",\"Generic filter-branch or filter-repo warnings without a validated exact mutating predicate\"],\"focusTrack\":\"noise-calibration-final-matrix\",\"edgeCase\":\"missing-dependency\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Skill\",\"Glob\",\"Read\",\"Bash\",\"ApplyPatch\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\"research/BRIEFING.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json\",\"research/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl\",\"research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\",\"research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-001.jsonl\",\"research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-002.jsonl\",\"research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-003.jso... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n2: {\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"f5-final-retained-matrix\",\"summary\":\"Retain 23 exact command/state rules ranked by positive evidence and failure cost; coalesce overlapping remote, recovery, staging, and coordination facts.\"}\n3: {\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"f5-final-rejections\",\"summary\":\"Reject broad families, unavailable ownership/outcome predicates, enforcement duplicates, and routine or built-in-protected forms.\"}\n4: {\"type\":\"observation\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"o5-probe-latency\",\"normalBudgetMs\":750,\"exceptionalCleanBudgetMs\":3500,\"allWorktreeSweepMs\":20147.45,\"statusMedianMs\":464.68,\"commitDryRunMedianMs\":601.58,\"cleanIgnoredMedianMs\":1630.21}\n5: {\"type\":\"invariant\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"i5-attention-budget\",\"summary\":\"At most one 180-character advisory line per Bash invocation; target below 0.5 alerts per 100 invocations per rule and below 2 per 100 aggregate, with hard ceilings of 1 and 3 respectively.\"}\n6: {\"type\":\"observation\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"o5-measurement-boundary\",\"summary\":\"Option-sensitive historical fire rates remain unmeasured; future normalized shadow telemetry is required and must exclude raw commands, paths, refs, URLs, and credentials.\"}\n\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":5,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":5,\"status\":\"complete\",\"focus\":\"Calibrate the final candidate matrix and noise threshold into a decision-ready rule set\",\"findingsCount\":5,\"newInfoRatio\":0.8,\"noveltyJustification\":\"2 of 5 findings were fully new and 3 partially new, yielding 0.70 plus a 0.10 simplicity bonus for resolving the final open question.\",\"keyQuestions\":[\"How often would each candidate fire in real repository history, and what is the defensible noise threshold?\"],\"answeredQuestions\":[\"How often can retained candidates legitimately be measured from existing history, where should the noise threshold sit, and what final ranked rule set should advance?\"],\"ruledOut\":[\"Broad Git-family, path-count, and ownership-inference warnings\",\"Predicates requiring post-fetch, post-hook, transport-credential, authorization, or final remote outcome state\",\"Duplicate naming and permission advisories already owned by pre-push enforcement\",\"Network probes, full object scans, and all-worktree sweeps in the synchronous hot path\",\"Generic filter-branch or filter-repo warnings without a validated exact mutating predicate\"],\"focusTrack\":\"noise-calibration-final-matrix\",\"edgeCase\":\"missing-dependency\",\"toolsUsed\":[\"Skill\",\"Glob\",\"Read\",\"Bash\",\"ApplyPatch\"],\"sourcesQueried\":[\"research/BRIEFING.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json\",\"research/lineages/sol/deep-research-state.jsonl\",\"research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\",\"research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-001.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-002.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-003.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/iterations/iteration-004.md\",\"research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-001.jsonl\",\"research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-002.jsonl\",\"research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-003.jso... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"f5-final-retained-matrix\",\"summary\":\"Retain 23 exact command/state rules ranked by positive evidence and failure cost; coalesce overlapping remote, recovery, staging, and coordination facts.\"}\n{\"type\":\"finding\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"f5-final-rejections\",\"summary\":\"Reject broad families, unavailable ownership/outcome predicates, enforcement duplicates, and routine or built-in-protected forms.\"}\n{\"type\":\"observation\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"o5-probe-latency\",\"normalBudgetMs\":750,\"exceptionalCleanBudgetMs\":3500,\"allWorktreeSweepMs\":20147.45,\"statusMedianMs\":464.68,\"commitDryRunMedianMs\":601.58,\"cleanIgnoredMedianMs\":1630.21}\n{\"type\":\"invariant\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"i5-attention-budget\",\"summary\":\"At most one 180-character advisory line per Bash invocation; target below 0.5 alerts per 100 invocations per rule and below 2 per 100 aggregate, with hard ceilings of 1 and 3 respectively.\"}\n{\"type\":\"observation\",\"iteration\":5,\"id\":\"o5-measurement-boundary\",\"summary\":\"Option-sensitive historical fire rates remain unmeasured; future normalized shadow telemetry is required and must exclude raw commands, paths, refs, URLs, and credentials.\"}","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deltas/iter-005.jsonl","text":"{\"type\":\"iteration\",\"iteration\":5,\"mode\":\"research\",\"target_agent\":\"deep-research\",\"agent_definition_loaded\":true,\"resolved_route\":\"Resolved route: mode=research target_agent=deep-research\",\"run\":