{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1785181594723,"sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_XsX5PZ6J3VmpQ4zzuzgutmW8","state":{"status":"error","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-config.json\n@@\n-  \"status\": \"initialized\",\n+  \"status\": \"complete\",\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@\n-- [ ] How often would each candidate fire in real repository history, and what is the defensible noise threshold?\n+- [x] How often would each candidate fire in real repository history, and what is the defensible noise threshold?\n@@\n - Which dangerous-looking operations should remain silent because enforcement already owns them or preflight state is unavailable/too noisy?\n+- How existing history can and cannot measure candidate frequency, where the provisional noise threshold sits, and which ranked set should advance to shadow mode.\n@@\n - Resolving actual worktree, destination, account, environment, hook, and ref state separated deterministic local push consequences from authorization guesses. (iteration 4)\n+- Reusing prior evidence while benchmarking only probe latency produced a ranked 23-rule matrix, explicit rejection set, and measurable shadow-mode attention budget. (iteration 5)\n@@\n - Push history has no argv/failure record, and network reads cannot close receive-time races; current missing hook installation is a health issue rather than advisory ownership evidence. (iteration 4)\n+- Existing Git history cannot provide option-sensitive fire rates; the final calibration therefore requires normalized future PreToolUse telemetry rather than another history pass. (iteration 5)\n@@\n - Generic push/account/worktree/multi-ref warnings and duplicate naming/permission advisories: positive local evidence or uncovered semantics are required. (iteration 4)\n+- Network probes, full object scans, all-worktree status sweeps, and generic filter-rewrite name matching are outside the synchronous advisory budget. (iteration 5)\n@@\n - Treating `gh` identity, API permission, leases, or remote snapshots as proof of Git transport identity, authorization, or final push outcome. (iteration 4)\n+- Broad operation/path-count/ownership warnings and every predicate requiring post-fetch, post-hook, transport, authorization, or final outcome state. (iteration 5)\n@@\n - What final candidate tiers, coalescing rules, latency limits, and aggregate alert budget keep advisories below the attention threshold? (iteration 4)\n+- No key research questions remain. Implementation must validate the retained classifier in privacy-preserving shadow mode. (iteration 5)\n@@\n ## 11. NEXT FOCUS\n-Calibrate the final candidate matrix and noise threshold: rank all retained rules by positive-evidence strength and overlap, measure available repository-history proxies, define one-line coalescing and latency budgets, and explicitly reject rules whose exact fire rate is unmeasured or likely too high.\n+[All tracked questions are resolved]\n*** Update File: .opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/findings-registry.json\n@@\n-  \"openQuestions\": [\"q-noise\"],\n-  \"resolvedQuestions\": [\"q-operation-families\", \"q-prestate\", \"q-new-rules\", \"q-silence\"],\n+  \"terminalStop\": {\n+    \"stopReason\": \"maxIterationsReached\",\n+    \"totalIterations\": 5,\n+    \"answeredCount\": 5,\n+    \"totalQuestions\": 5,\n+    \"timestamp\": \"2026-07-27T19:41:12Z\"\n+  },\n+  \"openQuestions\": [],\n+  \"resolvedQuestions\": [\"q-operation-families\", \"q-prestate\", \"q-new-rules\", \"q-noise\", \"q-silence\"],\n@@\n     {\n       \"id\": \"f4-uncovered-refspecs\",\n       \"iteration\": 4,\n       \"text\": \"Current pre-push enforcement skips tags and does not own force/delete/mirror/prune or destructive multi-ref semantics; these require positive destination evidence and coalesced advisories.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"f5-final-matrix\",\n+      \"iteration\": 5,\n+      \"text\": \"Twenty-three exact command/state rules survive ranking; fourteen broad, unavailable, enforcement-owned, or over-budget classes are rejected.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"id\": \"f5-attention-budget\",\n+      \"iteration\": 5,\n+      \"text\": \"Shadow-mode targets are under 0.5 alerts per 100 eligible invocations per rule and under 2 per 100 aggregate, with hard ceilings of 1 and 3; emit one coalesced line at most.\"\n@@\n-    \"iterationsCompleted\": 4,\n-    \"openQuestions\": 1,\n-    \"resolvedQuestions\": 4,\n-    \"keyFindings\": 41,\n-    \"convergenceScore\": 0.75,\n-    \"coverageBySources\": {\"code\": 33, \"history\": 16, \"state\": 26, \"web\": 2, \"network\": 2}\n+    \"iterationsCompleted\": 5,\n+    \"openQuestions\": 0,\n+    \"resolvedQuestions\": 5,\n+    \"keyFindings\": 46,\n+    \"convergenceScore\": 0.8,\n+    \"coverageBySources\": {\"code\": 33, \"history\": 20, \"state\": 30, \"web\": 2, \"network\": 2, \"benchmark\": 13}\n*** End Patch"},"error":"apply_patch verification failed: Error: Failed to find expected lines in /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.opencode/specs/sk-git/016-git-action-advisory-hook/001-advisory-research/research/lineages/sol/deep-research-strategy.md:\n- Which dangerous-looking operations should remain silent because enforcement already owns them or preflight state is unavailable/too noisy?","time":{"start":1785181594713,"end":1785181594721}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0aa680fb98fd1485016a67b58571ec819191ddae58db66b35d"}},"id":"prt_fa51d11c0001aq92I71YYtiJ3S","sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","messageID":"msg_fa51cde530011d8LheaFZKW272"}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1785181595871,"sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","part":{"id":"prt_fa51d68dd001I0E8CP8eIGxO61","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"fe03b20dde9c4dbba7dc0e6f79ecce2c3c838fcc","messageID":"msg_fa51cde530011d8LheaFZKW272","sessionID":"ses_05b144ddbffeTP8bqXDQv88HuN","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":268164,"input":13005,"output":1297,"reasoning":422,"cache":{"write":0,"read":253440}},"cost":0}}
